24,"kind":{"StorageDead":378},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":1052},"id":8593,"kind":"Return","comments_before":[]}]},"comments":[[163,["we read 8 bytes at a time (u64) but only actually consume 6 of those bytes. Thus, we need","2 trailing bytes to be available to read.."]],[169,["Major performance wins from letting the optimizer do the bounds check once, mostly","on the output side"]],[179,["Hand-unrolling for 32 vs 16 or 8 bytes produces yields performance about equivalent","to unsafe pointer code on a Xeon E5-1650v3. 64 byte unrolling was slightly better for","large inputs but significantly worse for 50-byte input, unsurprisingly. I suspect","that it's a not uncommon use case to encode smallish chunks of data (e.g. a 64-byte","SHA-512 digest), so it would be nice if that fit in the unrolled loop at least once.","Plus, single-digit percentage performance differences might well be quite different","on different hardware."]],[230,["Encode what's left after the fast loop."]],[237,["start at the first index not handled by fast loop, which may be 0."]]]}}},{"def_id":54,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["base64",0]},{"Ident":["engine",0]},{"Ident":["general_purpose",0]},{"Impl":{"Trait":6}},{"Ident":["internal_decode",0]},{"Impl":{"Trait":12}},{"Ident":["call_once",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":9,"beg":{"line":107,"col":12},"end":{"line":107,"col":28}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":"|_, _, _| (0, 0)","attr_info":{"attributes":[],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":false},"is_local":true,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"},{"index":1,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_